WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.290
Hi, I'm Flint!

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:03.957
Jev only makes typed decisions.

00:00:03.957 --> 00:00:07.292
This week, people pointed it at things that aren't decisions.

00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:13.618
Ask one independent Choice per pixel, and paint the answers.

00:00:13.618 --> 00:00:17.689
The picture comes from the marginals alone, and the brushwork maps doubt.

00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:24.266
Jev-paint writes one block of state, the prompt and the grid.

00:00:24.266 --> 00:00:26.909
Then it asks one sixteen-colour Choice per pixel.

00:00:27.329 --> 00:00:28.959
No question sees another.

00:00:28.959 --> 00:00:33.850
Thirty-two by thirty-two is a thousand and twenty-four questions, in eight requests.

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:35.326
Back come distributions.

00:00:35.326 --> 00:00:39.198
At twelve by twelve, their top picks already form a sunflower.

00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:43.545
The renderer turns each distribution into one number.

00:00:43.965 --> 00:00:45.100
Take its entropy, H.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.936
E to the H counts the colours effectively in play.

00:00:48.356 --> 00:00:51.387
Low spread, a confident pixel, gets a wider brush.

00:00:51.986 --> 00:00:56.134
But below a spread of zero point four eight, no stroke is drawn.

00:00:56.134 --> 00:00:59.325
The widest brush never touches the canvas; texture marks doubt.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:04.491
A robot run asks two questions per cycle: which of eight intents,

00:01:04.491 --> 00:01:05.772
like grasp or lift,

00:01:06.192 --> 00:01:09.227
then which way to nudge each axis and the gripper.

00:01:09.227 --> 00:01:11.352
A shared executor does the actual motion.

00:01:11.772 --> 00:01:15.090
The loop runs at zero point six two hertz, and eighty-seven point

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.579
nine percent of that is waiting on the calls.

00:01:18.758 --> 00:01:22.886
And Jesse v1, with no weights, claims a hundred percent on HumanEval.

00:01:22.886 --> 00:01:26.669
On SWE-bench, all five of its non-empty patches are the gold

00:01:26.669 --> 00:01:28.045
patches, byte for byte.

00:01:29.517 --> 00:01:31.636
In all three, the interface gets measured.

00:01:31.636 --> 00:01:35.573
The number is almost never the finding; the shape of the question is.

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:41.089
To recap: independent Choices paint, the gate maps doubt, and round trips

00:01:41.089 --> 00:01:42.429
set the robot's pace.

00:01:42.849 --> 00:01:44.907
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:44.907 --> 00:01:45.495
I'm Flint.

00:01:45.495 --> 00:01:45.789
Bye!
